  "narrative": "The new validation evidence confirms the clean feature_063 claim but rejects the sparse conditional feature_063 claim. For H55, the validation result is signed +0.281 with interval [0.159,0.403]; the lower bound exceeds the 0.15 threshold, although only modestly. Combined with discovery +0.252 [0.169,0.335], this supports a dataset-specific association in which feature_063=1 versus 0 is associated with stronger composite dependency in the triple-strong-absent stratum feature_037=0, feature_010=0, feature_002=0. I accept it but close the exact investigation because this targeted validation is the direct evidence for that exact claim; the margin above threshold is not large enough to overstate generalizability. For H75, discovery gave +0.365 [0.180,0.550], but stringent validation gave +0.347 [0.072,0.623]. The point estimate remains directionally consistent and relatively large, but the validation interval crosses the 0.15 threshold and the exposed cell is only 44 observations. The exact claim that feature_063=1 is associated with stronger dependency among feature_002=1 participants therefore remains unresolved rather than accepted. I close this exact investigation because further same-dataset contrasts would add multiplicity without directly fixing the validation-threshold uncertainty. For H7, the validation for the feature_058-by-feature_018 interaction is signed +0.082 [-0.115,0.280], below threshold and compatible with null; combined with the discovery estimate -0.089 [-0.225,0.047], the evidence does not support a threshold-exceeding interaction. I keep H7 rejected and closed. Overall, the supported dataset-specific structure remains: feature_037=1 is robustly associated with stronger dependency, and feature_010=1 and feature_002=1 are robustly associated with weaker dependency; tested pairwise interactions and log_PFS attenuation are unsupported. For feature_063, only the clean triple-strong-absent H55 is secure; broader or sparse conditional feature_063 claims, including H75, remain near-threshold or underpowered. Negative findings include feature_007, feature_058, feature_015, several research-signature subgroup claims, many low-prevalence binary markers, the feature_046 categorical probe, and now the feature_058-by-feature_018 interaction. feature_003 remains a consistent near-threshold candidate but not accepted. The most informative next analysis is to resolve the new feature_027 signal already accepted overall in H35 by examining H83 and H84. If feature_027 remains large in the triple-strong-absent stratum and in the feature_037=0 complement, it would become a second strong dataset-specific marker candidate; if attenuated or null, its large marginal contrast is probably tied to overlap with feature_037 or other dominant predictors. After that, conditional feature_027 analyses with the weaker-dependency markers and limited categorical coverage probes are the next best use of slots.",
  "research_notes": "Updated after H55/H75/H7 validation responses.\n\nStrong accepted core:\n- H15: feature_037=1 associated with much stronger dependency; discovery +0.804 [0.742,0.867], validation +0.800 [0.705,0.895]; accepted and closed.\n- feature_010=1 and feature_002=1: accepted large weaker-dependency associations overall and in many complement/overlap conditionals. H76/H77 show feature_010 and feature_002 contrasts remain very large among feature_063=1 participants.\n- H55: feature_063=1 associated with stronger dependency in feature_037=0, feature_010=0, feature_002=0; discovery +0.252 [0.169,0.335], validation +0.281 [0.159,0.403]; accepted and closed, but lower bound only modestly above threshold.\n\nRecent validation changes:\n- H75 downgraded from accept to unresolved/closed. Discovery +0.365 [0.180,0.550] among feature_002=1, but validation +0.347 [0.072,0.623]; validation lower bound below 0.15 and exposed n=44. Direction replicated but threshold not independently established.\n- H7 remains reject/closed. Discovery feature_058-by-feature_018 interaction -0.089 [-0.225,0.047]; validation +0.082 [-0.115,0.280]; no threshold support.\n\nCurrent candidate to resolve:\n- H35 feature_027=1 associated with stronger dependency overall: +0.775 [0.664,0.885], exposed n=130. This is accepted but needs conditional confirmation.\n- H83 (feature_027 in triple-strong-absent stratum) and H84 (feature_027 in feature_037=0 complement) are the highest-priority next analyses.\n\nUnresolved near-threshold/low-confidence:\n- feature_063 conditionals outside H55: H52/H69 discovery-only conditional supports; H51 and H73 unresolved/closed after validation crossed threshold; H74 unresolved/deferred in feature_010=1; H68/H70 deferred due imprecision or interval crossing null/threshold.\n- feature_003 consistently positive-signed but lower bounds below threshold in H18/H53/H59/H72; do not promote.\n- H29/H35 follow-ups and categorical H79-H82 remain possible coverage analyses if feature_027 is resolved.\n\nNext analyze priority:\n1. Analyze H83 and H84 for feature_027 conditional independence from dominant predictors.\n2. If feature_027 remains large in clean/feature_037=0 strata, consider feature_027 as a strong dataset-specific candidate and maybe targeted validation or interaction/overlap analyses.\n3. If feature_027 attenuates/nulls, interpret H35 as likely correlated with feature_037/dominant structure and close or deprioritize.\n4. Only then consider broader categorical probes or additional feature_063 refinements; feature_003 should not receive extra slots unless a threshold-exceeding conditional appears."
